{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected control assesses one identified benefit offered by one distributor in the SFC-authorised-fund context.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Separately identifiable benefits in a combined offer are assessed separately; identifying those benefits may require judgment.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Gift classification, discount classification and promotional linkage are supplied judgments, not inferred from a benefit’s label or from the mere existence of additional returns.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The result is interpreted only when scope is true; unknown facts remain unknown.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"fd1353007afb88c6117d9461019ca0bb0eff6dfc020965979cd65f2c62c6ed1f","candidate_id":"candidate.55f047612bfb47fe948ec30a02536704","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] For the selected control, Paragraph 3.11 gift restriction for one offered benefit, true means that the in-scope benefit is either not a gift or qualifies for the fee-or-charge discount exception. False means that it is an in-scope gift outside that exception and fails the stated should-not-offer standard. This is a proposed interpretation of that control only; it does not determine compliance of other offer components, section 103 compliance or whole-firm compliance.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["exceptions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The discount exception applies to the identified benefit, while product-type promotion remains covered. For example, an offer promoting funds of one fund house could combine a fee reduction with a separately identifiable shopping voucher. Assuming the voucher is a gift and not a fee discount, the fee reduction satisfies this control and the voucher fails it. The text does not support exempting the entire package because one component is a discount, or excluding it because no individual fund is singled out. A fee-linked cash rebate presents a genuine unresolved classification question: if it is a discount it satisfies this control; if it is a non-discount gift it fails. The packet does not supply enough criteria to choose between those classifications.","run_id":"run.0df6ab9ed0764d18b4c54714bd84a275","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"9cc272f84dbcec164f1a7a7a567859d8a6feb7fc34af22d7bef3e7688f64f736","source_unit_ids":["db43e253bea18.u0.2","db43e253bea18.u12.2646","db43e253bea18.u13.2987","db43e253bea18.u14.3675","db43e253bea18.u7.1360"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"A separately identified benefit offered by a distributor during promotion to a client"}